Thanks to Steve LaBelle, Chris Wincentsen, and John Lanier for quick
replies.

As stated before, I added the entry back in the /etc/passwd file.
Typing in edauth adm showed that there was an entry there for the
acccount so I didn't have to run convuser.  I then ran pwck and grpck
and found that adm had no password, which I took care of.

I think we're good to go.

Thanks again all and happy Friday!  (7.5 hours 'til beer thirty) =20

